<title>UK: Southern Company unit sets $300 mln 40-year bond.</title>
<headline>Southern Company unit sets $300 mln 40-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Lehman and Goldman Sachs International.  BORROWER   SOUTHERN COMPANY CAPITAL TRUST 1</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  SOUTHERN COMPANY</p>
<p> AMT    $300 MLN	COUPON     **	  MATURITY    01.FEB.37</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  **	  PAY DATE    31.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.00	LISTING    NONE	PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> NOTES	**TO BE PRICED		     SPREAD     +125 BP</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  A3/A-     DENOMS (K) =	   SALE LIMITS =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 30-YEAR U.S TREASURY</p>
<p> NOTES	CALLABLE AT PAR IN 2007</p>
<p>		SUBORDINATED CAPITAL INCOME SECURITIES DEAL</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
